{"id": "EUVD-2026-107893", "enisaUuid": "5c9581f1-eef2-37b9-ad48-1d19bd986bd3", "description": "Traefik v3.7.0 before v3.7.14 contains an improper authentication vulnerability in the Kubernetes Ingress NGINX provider that merges client CAs when auth-tls-secret names collide after dot-to-dash normalization. Attackers holding certificates from another host's CA can access a host requiring its own client CA, while that host's legitimate clients are refused.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T01:43:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T01:43:38", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/traefik/traefik/security/advisories/GHSA-rv2h-qh7j-xrjw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/traefik-3.7.0-before-3.7.14-client-ca-mix-up-via-auth-tls-secret-name-collision"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114638", "GHSA-378g-rwj7-qp6j"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "96ec1fd3-e249-35b8-8660-df971c94b31d", "product": {"name": "traefik", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}, "product_version": "3.7.0 <3.7.14"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f043faeb-276f-3b44-b004-c522130e1f24", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}], "isExploited": false}